<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia posts $957.3 mln Jan-Aug C/A deficit.</title>
<headline>Slovakia posts $957.3 mln Jan-Aug C/A deficit.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak current account recorded a deficit for the January-August period of $957.3 million, compared with a $607.7 surplus over the same period last year, the central bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It added the capital acccount was in surplus in the first eight months of the year by $1.1 billion, compared with a surplus of $175.3 million in the same period last year.  </p>
<p> SLOVAK CURRENT ACCOUNT   8MO'96    7MO'96    8MO'95    FY/95</p>
<p>  overall ($million)	-957.3    -847.2    +607.7   +648.8</p>
<p>  trade balance	   -1,160.4  -1,048.0     +38.0    +24.1</p>
<p>  balance of services     +103.7    +102.1    +500.1   +546.2</p>
<p>  income balance	     +18.5     +25.3     +35.8    -13.7</p>
<p>  current transfers	  +80.8     +73.3     +33.7    +92.2</p>
<p>CAPITAL ACCOUNT</p>
<p>Total Capital and financial</p>
<p> account balance	  +1,111.5    +949.9    +175.3   +993.9</p>
<p> capital transfers	   +29.9     +29.9     +45.7    +45.7</p>
<p>direct investment balance</p>
<p>  inv. in Slovak republic  +68.9     +98.1     +75.7   +141.9</p>
<p>  Slovak investment abroad  -8.4	-8.2	-5.3     -7.9</p>
<p>portfolio investment balance</p>
<p>  inv. in Slovak Republic  +12.1	+9.9     +11.3    +74.4</p>
<p>  Slovak investment abroad +85.3     +49.9     +87.0   +171.7</p>
<p>other long-term financial</p>
<p>  account		     +417.8    +352.1    +102.5   +393.8</p>
<p> short-term fin. account  +505.9    +418.1    -168.6    +91.3</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in millions of U.S. dollars. Figures</p>
<p>are subject to parliamentary approval. The central bank used</p>
<p>the following exchange rates in calculating the figures:</p>
<p>Jan-Aug '96 (USD=30.427 SKK), Jan-July'96 (USD=30.435 SKK),</p>
<p>full year '95 (USD=29.735 SKK), Jan-Aug '95 (USD=29.761).</p>
<p>-- Tatiana Vacova, Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-536-3687</p>
